{"description":"Complete eka-steward's design-system alignment: 2.2.0 themed only the run report and the version command, so the help surface (--help / \u003ccmd\u003e --help) and the bare --version flag still rendered raw cobra / plain text with no left margin and no color. Added internal/ui/container.go (the output container: uniform left margin + leading/trailing blank line), cmd/help_render.go (the CLI's own help renderer — command names info, flag names + trailing hint dim — wired as the root HelpFunc and wrapped in ui.Container so help resolves up the tree for every command), and dropped the root Long's hand-written command block now duplicated by cobra's rendered Available Commands:. cmd/root.go now sets root.SetHelpFunc and prints --version through styleFor(c).W. Non-TTY output stays plain text with no ANSI (colors only on a color TTY; NO_COLOR / TERM=dumb respected); run --json and the machine surface are byte-unchanged. Shipped as eka-steward v2.2.1 (patch).","acceptanceCriteria":"gofmt -l empty, go vet clean, GOOS=windows build ok, go test -race -count=1 ./... all packages ok. PR #5 merged to develop. Tag v2.2.1 released with all assets (eka-steward-{linux,darwin,windows}-{amd64,arm64}[.exe], install.sh, install.ps1, SHA256SUMS.txt). Released binary: --help renders with the leading blank line and the two-space left margin on every line and NO ANSI on a non-TTY, and with ANSI color on a PTY; --version prints the bare version margin-indented; version prints 'eka-steward 2.2.1' + 'eka-core api v1'."}